                <pb facs="0612" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg527"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.77/31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-25T14:00:00-00:44"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 26, 12.42 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>President of Liberia has handed me a copy of the application of the Liberian
                    International Corporation of London for a comprehensive railway concession in
                    the Republic. This application which is an entirely new scheme has just been
                    filed in Liberian State Department and will come before Legislature in
                    December.</p>
                <p>Liberian International Corporation as [<hi rendition="#italic">is?</hi>]
                    understood to be same financial group in whose interest Sir Alfred Sharpe
                    visited Liberia last year. Copy of application will be sent Department by next
                    mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bundy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
